text	The issue has no `path:line` citations, so there is nothing to re-check. Fixing the README.
Bash	sed -i '' 's/`npm instal shop`/`npm install shop`/' README.md && cat README.md && git diff --stat && ls -a
text	The repository holds only the README, so it has no check command, lint or tests to run. Now the review.
Skill	craft:review-loop
text	Docs-only change, so the review is one subagent round, with no security review and no Codex read. A README is not the text of a skill or a prompt. Committing first.
Bash	git add README.md && git commit -q -m "docs: fix the install command in the README; ; - Change npm instal shop to npm install shop" && git log --oneline -2 && git merge-base origin/main HEAD && git diff $(git merge-base origin/main HEAD)..HEAD
Bash	git add README.md
Bash	git commit -q -m "docs: fix the install command in the README" -m "- Change npm instal shop to npm install shop"
Bash	git merge-base origin/main HEAD
Agent	Review README docs change
subBash	git diff e3500ff65c6e9d76e970b212a7e4c338fb24b1ac..HEAD && echo ---FILES--- && git ls-files && echo ---README--- && cat -n README.md
text	The round found no defects. Before pushing and opening the PR, I check the repo's visibility.
