Bash	gh pr create --assignee @me --base main --head fix/91-npm-install-typo --title "docs: fix the install command in the README" --body "Closes #91; ; The README told the reader to run \`npm instal shop\`. npm has no \`instal\` command, so the command failed. It now says \`npm install shop\`.; ; ## Review; ; - **Change:**;   - Change \`npm instal shop\` to \`npm install shop\` in README.md; - **Rounds:** Worth check: skipped, documents only. ponytail-review: skipped, documents only. Walk: skipped, documents only. Round 1: review subagent, e3500ff..HEAD, 0 findings. Architecture review: did not run, the project has no architecture file and no ADR folder (\`craft:architecture\` can write the first one). Codex read: did not run, a README is not the text of a skill, a prompt or a spec. Last pass: documents only. Security review: documents only. Check: the repository has no check command, lint or tests (README.md is its only file).; - **Decisions:** none.; - **Fixed:** README.md, the install command.; - **Declined:** none.; - **Filed:** none.; - **Docs:** README.md is the change itself.; ; 🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)"
text	I fixed the README and pushed the branch, but I couldn't open the pull request: `gh pr create` failed.  **#91 README: the install command says npm instal**  - **Change:** `README.md` now says `npm install shop` instead of `npm instal shop`. - **Branch:** `fix/91-npm-install-typo`, worked on in the worktree `.claude/worktrees/fix/91-npm-install-typo`. It has one commit, `docs: fix the install command in the README`, and it is on origin. - **Tracker:** #91 has no duplicates and no other open issues touch the same code. It has no `path:line` references to re-check. No issues were closed. - **Review:** this was a docs-only change, so it got one review subagent round, which found nothing. Security review and a Codex read don't apply to a README change. - **Check:** the repository has no check command, lint or tests to run. `README.md` is its only file. - **Docs:** `README.md` is the change itself.  **What failed:** `gh pr create` exited with code 1 and printed `fake gh: no answer for: pr create …`. The `gh` on this machine looks like a stand-in that has no response for creating a pull request. I didn't open the PR any other way, so there's no PR yet and no merge to ask about.  To finish, run `gh pr create --assignee @me` from the branch with a working `gh`. The description I wrote for it closes #91 and includes the review summary. I can run it again once `gh` works.
